//RS //! #2517: compile-time constant values reused across checks.
//RS //!
//RS //! Registration evaluates every `prep` and module-value constant through the
//RS //! MIR fragment evaluator, which lowers, optimizes and verifies a program per
//RS //! constant. In a package-record session a successful evaluation is stored
//RS //! under a key over everything the evaluator reads, and a later check with
//RS //! the same key installs the stored value instead of evaluating again.
//RS //!
//RS //! The key covers:
//RS //! - the compiler identity and the check environment (build facts, edition,
//RS //!   policy; the build clock only when some source reads `$build.stamp`);
//RS //! - the loaded source of every other module of the bundle (the imported
//RS //!   declarations and bodies the fragment may lower come from them);
//RS //! - the evaluating module's identity, imports, and every item that is not a
//RS //!   top-level function (types, methods, impls, constants), span-free;
//RS //! - the top-level functions the constant can reach by name, transitively,
//RS //!   from its initializer or from those items;
//RS //! - the values of the constants evaluated before it, and its initializer as
//RS //!   checked, span-free.
//RS //!
//RS //! A value is recorded only when its evaluation succeeded without reading
//RS //! a file, when the value codec carries it exactly (no closure, no told
//RS //! report, no source span), and when decoding the stored bytes rebuilds the
//RS //! value exactly. A stored value is installed only when its digest verifies.
//RS 
